        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Sunny high ground, rocky ledges, and ruined fortresses"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A giant milk-white snake with a gold mane of facial hair, long fangs, multifaceted eyes, and translucent patches that show veins."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Special attacks mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Whistling charm · The snake whistles to draw a target to it. The target makes a save vs. Spell. The snake’s first successful strike against that target ends the charm. The bite is nonvenomous."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Encounters mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Room 29, ballroom · The snake hides in the suspended bell with 16 HP. Every creature that hears its whistle must save vs. Spell or be charmed."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "1–4 appearing. Saves as Fighter 3. Morale 8. Treasure type C. Neutral.",
            "Jean Wells, Palace of the Silver Princess (orange cover, TSR, 1981), pp. 25 and 27."
          ]
        }
