          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A giant jungle monkey with a sharp, furry tail spike. The two Cell D guards are 8 feet tall when upright and have 12-foot tails."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Attacks mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Claws, bite, and tail spike · The printed damage sequence is 1–6, 1–6, 1–8, and 1–4. The marmoset uses the 1–4 tail spike on the ground. In the trees, it hangs by its tail and fights with its claws and bite.",
            "Thrown stones · From cliffs the marmosets prefer to throw large stones at prey below. The entry gives no damage or range for the stones."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Encounters mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Room 32, Cell D · Two Chaotic guards with 10 HP each attack anyone who enters except Travis. The general profile lists Neutral."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "2–8 appearing. Saves as Fighter 3. Morale 8. Treasure type J. Neutral.",
            "Jean Wells, Palace of the Silver Princess (orange cover, TSR, 1981), pp. 16 and 28."
